{"timestamp": 1779376190.8381681, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I found Frank's body in upper engine, just now. I also need to flag that I saw Diana's body in medbay on my way through \u2014 she came in from storage at tick 18 while Bob was also in medbay with me. I left medbay heading to electrical, then came back through medbay to upper engine where I found Frank.\n\nMy route was: navigation -> security -> weapons -> cafeteria -> medbay -> electrical -> medbay -> upper_engine.\n\nI saw Charlie in weapons early (ticks 4-5), Eve was in electrical for a while (ticks 15-17), and Eve had entered medbay from upper engine at tick 11. Bob and Diana were both with me in medbay at tick 18.\n\nBob is suspicious to me \u2014 he was in medbay with Diana right before she died. I'd like to hear his account. Also Eve was moving between upper engine and electrical, which puts her near both bodies."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376201.674602, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Thanks Alice. Let me give my route: upper_engine -> oxygen -> upper_engine -> medbay -> electrical, then I was in security when the meeting was called.\n\nHere's what I saw:\n- Tick 5: Frank was with me in oxygen. At tick 6 Frank left oxygen heading to upper_engine.\n- Tick 8: Bob entered oxygen from cafeteria while I was there.\n- Tick 9: I moved to upper_engine and saw Frank, Bob, AND Diana all there together.\n- Tick 13: I was in medbay and saw Charlie there.\n- Tick 14: Bob entered medbay from cafeteria \u2014 wait, that's odd because Alice said Bob was in medbay with her at tick 18. Bob was moving around a lot.\n- Ticks 15-17: I was in electrical, and Alice was there with me the whole time. So Alice has a solid alibi for that window.\n\nOne correction to Alice: she said I entered medbay from upper_engine at tick 11 \u2014 that matches my route (upper_engine -> medbay around then). And I was in electrical 15-17 WITH Alice, so we can vouch for each other in that window.\n\nFrank died in upper_engine. At tick 9 I saw Frank, Bob, and Diana all in upper_engine together. After I left to medbay, any of them could have been the last with Frank. Bob then showed up in medbay at tick 14, and Alice says Diana died in medbay around tick 18 with Bob present.\n\nBob's movement pattern \u2014 upper_engine (with Frank/Diana) -> oxygen -> medbay -> medbay again \u2014 puts him at BOTH crime scenes. I'm leaning Bob. Let's hear him out."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376212.738388, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Okay, I need to address this directly because there are some inaccuracies in what's been said.\n\nMy actual route was: electrical -> medbay -> cafeteria -> oxygen -> upper_engine -> oxygen -> cafeteria -> medbay. I was NOT in medbay at tick 14, Eve \u2014 I was in cafeteria or oxygen around then. Please double-check your memory because that's a serious accusation built on a wrong tick.\n\nHere's what I actually saw:\n- Tick 9: I was in upper_engine with Frank, Diana, and Eve \u2014 all four of us were there together. So Eve is right that we were all in that room.\n- Tick 10: I was still in upper_engine, Frank was still alive. Then I left back toward oxygen.\n- Tick 18: I was in medbay when Diana entered from storage, and Alice was there too. Alice then LEFT medbay heading to upper_engine at tick 18. I also left medbay around then.\n\nImportant point: Alice says she \"left medbay heading to electrical, then came back through medbay to upper_engine where I found Frank.\" But I witnessed Alice leaving medbay directly toward upper_engine at tick 18 \u2014 right after Diana arrived. That means Alice was alone with Diana last, and then conveniently \"discovered\" Frank's body in upper_engine.\n\nEve and Alice are vouching for each other on the 15-17 electrical window, which is fine, but that doesn't cover the Diana kill. Diana died in medbay around tick 18, and Alice was the last person with her before reporting.\n\nI'm leaning Alice. Her story has her bouncing between both crime scenes and \"finding\" both bodies."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376230.163024, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Okay, I'm last so let me try to synthesize what we have.\n\nMy route was: security -> weapons -> cafeteria -> electrical -> medbay -> storage. I was NOT in weapons at ticks 4-5 the way Alice described it \u2014 well, actually I was, she's right about that. Alice entered weapons from security at tick 3 and was with me there at ticks 4-5. So Alice's early route checks out with mine.\n\nAt tick 13 I was in medbay and saw BOTH Alice and Eve there. That matches both their accounts \u2014 Eve says she was in medbay around then with me, and Alice's route has her passing through medbay. Good.\n\nAt tick 16 I saw Diana enter storage from lower_engine. So Diana was alive in storage at tick 16, then per Alice she entered medbay from storage at tick 18. That timeline works.\n\nNow the key conflict: Bob claims he was in electrical -> medbay -> cafeteria -> oxygen -> upper_engine -> oxygen -> cafeteria -> medbay. But Eve placed Bob in oxygen at tick 8 (entering from cafeteria) and in upper_engine at tick 9 with Frank and Diana. Bob's own account confirms he was in upper_engine at ticks 9-10 with Frank alive. \n\nThe critical question: who was last with Frank in upper_engine? Bob admits being there ticks 9-10. Alice arrived at upper_engine at the END (finding the body). Eve left upper_engine to medbay around tick 10-11.\n\nBob's accusation against Alice is interesting but Alice and Eve vouch for each other 15-17 in electrical, and Alice's earlier route through weapons matches my sighting. Bob, meanwhile, was at upper_engine with Frank AND in medbay at tick 18 when Diana died \u2014 he's at both crime scenes.\n\nI'm leaning Bob. His route puts him at both kills, and he's trying to deflect to Alice whose alibi with Eve is solid."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376238.7728808, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Thanks everyone. I've already laid out my route and observations, but let me respond to Bob's accusation since the speeches have continued.\n\nBob, you're misrepresenting what happened. I did NOT leave medbay directly to upper_engine at tick 18. My route went medbay -> electrical -> medbay -> upper_engine. Eve confirms I was in electrical with her at ticks 15-17, which is BEFORE Diana even arrived in medbay at tick 18. After electrical, I came back through medbay (where you and Diana were), then continued to upper_engine and found Frank.\n\nAlso, Frank's body in upper_engine \u2014 Frank was killed well before tick 18. You admit you were in upper_engine with Frank at ticks 9-10. Eve left upper_engine to medbay at tick 11. That leaves you, Bob, as one of the last people with Frank alive.\n\nAnd Charlie's synthesis is correct: my weapons alibi at ticks 4-5 is confirmed by Charlie, my electrical alibi at 15-17 is confirmed by Eve. Bob is the one whose route puts him at both crime scenes \u2014 upper_engine with Frank, and medbay with Diana.\n\nI'm voting Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376246.7784011, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I've already given my main speech, but since I have another chance to weigh in, let me lock in my position.\n\nBob's claim that he wasn't in medbay at tick 14 is a direct contradiction with what I personally witnessed \u2014 I saw him enter medbay from cafeteria at tick 14. That's not a memory error on my part; that was a clear sighting. If Bob is lying about that, it's because he needs to hide his movements.\n\nBob's deflection to Alice doesn't hold up either. Alice was with me in electrical at ticks 15-17 \u2014 that's a solid mutual alibi covering the window right before Diana's death. Bob, on the other hand, was in upper_engine with Frank at ticks 9-10 (he admits this), and was in medbay around tick 14 (I saw him) and again at tick 18 when Diana died (he admits this too).\n\nCharlie's synthesis matches what I saw. Bob is at both crime scenes, and he's lying about tick 14 to cover it.\n\nI'm voting Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376261.580035, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Look, I hear you all, but the case against me is built on a single disputed sighting from Eve. Let me be very precise about tick 14.\n\nAt tick 14 I was in cafeteria moving toward oxygen \u2014 NOT entering medbay. Eve, I think you may be confusing me with someone else passing through, or the tick is off by a few. My route is consistent: after upper_engine ticks 9-10, I went back to oxygen, then cafeteria, then medbay at tick 18. I was never in medbay between tick 2 and tick 18.\n\nOn Frank: yes, I was in upper_engine ticks 9-10 with Frank, Diana, AND Eve. That's FOUR people in the room. Eve left to medbay around tick 11, and I left back toward oxygen. Frank was alive when I left. Anyone could have come back \u2014 including Eve, who admits bouncing between upper_engine and medbay.\n\nOn Diana: she entered medbay at tick 18 from storage. Alice was there, I was there. Then Alice left toward upper_engine at tick 18 \u2014 I watched her go. If Diana died in medbay at tick 18, then either I did it or Alice did it. Alice then \"conveniently\" finds Frank's body in upper_engine right after leaving Diana behind.\n\nHere's the thing that bothers me: Alice and Eve have a mutual alibi for 15-17, and now Eve is the one pushing the tick-14 medbay claim that contradicts my route. That's a tight pair vouching for each other while pinning both kills on me.\n\nCharlie, I respect your synthesis but you're trusting Eve's tick-14 claim as fact. It's not \u2014 it's her word against mine.\n\nI'm voting Eve. She placed herself at upper_engine right before Frank died, she's pushing a sighting of me that I dispute, and she and Alice are suspiciously coordinated."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376269.830318, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I'll keep this brief since I already gave my synthesis and the late speakers have just reinforced positions.\n\nBob's defense relies on Eve being wrong about tick 14, but Eve's sighting is specific and consistent with Bob's own admitted movements (he says he was in cafeteria around then, and medbay is adjacent). More importantly, Bob being at upper_engine with Frank ticks 9-10 is admitted, and he was in medbay at tick 18 when Diana died \u2014 that's confirmed by both Alice AND Bob himself.\n\nBob's pivot to voting Eve feels like desperation. Eve and Alice's mutual alibi at 15-17 in electrical is exactly the kind of alibi that's hardest to fake \u2014 two people independently corroborating each other in a specific room for a specific window. And Alice's earlier route through weapons is confirmed by me directly.\n\nBob is at both crime scenes by his own admission. That's the cleanest evidence we have.\n\nI'm voting Bob."}}
